> Module Form1099_rs
> Using Types
> Using Rounding as R

# Form 1099-R: pensions and annuities (Form 1040 lines 5a, 5b and 25b)

Catala module for Direct File `form1099Rs.xml` (issue #22, `scope.md`
section 3.4). It classifies every Form 1099-R the filer typed in, and computes
what the rest of the return reads from them:

- Form 1040 line 5a, "Pensions and annuities" (DF `income.xml`
  `/pensionsAndAnnuities`) and line 5b, "Taxable amount" (DF `income.xml`
  `/taxablePensionsAndAnnuities`);
- the 1099-R part of line 25b (DF `form1099Rs.xml`
  `/form1099RsFederalIncomeTaxWithheld`, one term of `/form1099Withholding`);
- the per-filer gross distributions of Form 8880 line 4 (DF
  `/primaryFiler1099RsReportedOnSaversCredit`,
  `/secondaryFiler1099RsReportedOnSaversCredit`);
- the knockout conditions that send 1099-R shapes Direct File does not
  support out of scope (conventions section 6).

Conventions: `catala/CONVENTIONS.md`. Inputs are complete (section 3): an empty
box is an explicit `$0`. A DF `Round` is `R.round_dollar` and is applied
exactly where the XML applies it.

Oracle: `oracle/facts.csv` rows `/pensionsAndAnnuities` (5a),
`/taxablePensionsAndAnnuitiesDisplay` (5b), `/form1099Withholding` (25b, in
scenarios with no other 1099), compared by `make difftest SCOPE=form1099_rs`
(mapping `difftest/mappings/form1099_rs.mjs`).

Wiring (done by the orchestrator, not here): `Form1099Rs.line_5b` feeds the
`taxable_pensions_and_annuities` plug-in slot of `Form1040` (line 5b);
`Form1099Rs.form_1099r_federal_income_tax_withheld` is one term of the
`other_1099_withholding` slot (line 25b); `Form1099Rs.line_5a` feeds line 5a /
Schedule R; the two `..._savers_gross_distributions` outputs feed Form 8880
line 4; `Form1099Rs.unsupported` is one term of the return's `unsupported`.

## Facts skipped

Not modelled (conventions section 2, last rows): payer name, TIN, address and
phone; recipient address choices; account number; box 11 first year of
designated Roth contributions; box 9b employee contributions and box 5; state
and local boxes 16 to 20 other than the two withholding amounts used by the
box 15 knockout; `nonstandardOrCorrectedChoice` and its MeF helpers;
`hasSeenLastAvailableScreen`, `isComplete`, `form1099RsIsComplete`,
`hasCompleted1099RSection`, the 1099-R feature flag facts
(`/is1099RFeatureFlagEnabled`, `/hasSome1099rFormsBeforeSectionEnabled`,
`/has1099rFormsAndFeatureIsNotEnabled`, which is `False`).

Validation-only facts that block submission but are not in `flow.xml`'s
`/flowIsKnockedOut` are not modelled either: `/hasMoreTaxThanDistributionsOn1099Rs`
and `/form1099Rs/secondaryFilerUsedWithoutMFJ` (the filers and filing status
modules own the second one).

## Shapes

### The distribution code (box 7)

Box 7 holds one or two characters. Direct File's regex accepts any of
`A-H J-N P-U W 1-9` (digits and letters, never `0`, `I`, `O`, `V`, `X`, `Y`,
`Z`) and forbids repeating the same character. Only six characters change
what this module does, so the type below keeps those six and folds every other
accepted character into `OtherCode`. Lower case is the same as upper case
(DF applies `ToUpper` and `Trim` first); the caller does that.

```catala-metadata
## One character of the box 7 distribution code.
declaration enumeration CodeChar:
  -- Code2
  -- Code4
  -- Code7
  -- CodeB
  -- CodeG
  -- CodeH
  -- OtherCode
```

### One Form 1099-R

```catala-metadata
## One Form 1099-R as the filer typed it.
## DF: the `/form1099Rs` collection.
declaration structure Form1099R:
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/filer
  data filer content Types.FilerRole
  # Box 7, as the characters typed, in order, no whitespace.
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableDistributionCode
  data distribution_code content list of CodeChar
  # Box 1. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableGrossDistribution
  data writable_gross_distribution content money
  # Box 2a. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableTaxableAmount
  data writable_taxable_amount content money
  # True when box 2a is empty and "taxable amount not determined" is not
  # checked. With complete inputs this is only ever true as a deliberate test
  # of the knockout. DF: the blank test inside
  # /form1099Rs/*/causesRetirementTaxableAmountNotDeterminedNotCheckedTaxableAmountBlankKO
  data taxable_amount_blank content boolean
  # Box 2b first checkbox. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableTaxableAmountNotDetermined
  data taxable_amount_not_determined content boolean
  # Box 2b second checkbox. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableTotalDistribution
  data total_distribution content boolean
  # Box 3. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableCapitalGain
  data writable_capital_gain content money
  # Box 4. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableFederalWithholding
  data writable_federal_withholding content money
  # Box 6. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableNetAppreciation
  data writable_net_appreciation content money
  # Box 7 IRA/SEP/SIMPLE checkbox. DF: /form1099Rs/*/iraSepSimple
  data ira_sep_simple content boolean
  # Box 8 dollar amount. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableOtherDollar
  data writable_other_dollar content money
  # Box 8 percentage is not zero: DF keeps the text typed and tests that it
  # holds some character other than `0` and `.`. The caller computes it.
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableOtherPercentage
  data other_percentage_nonzero content boolean
  # Box 9a percentage is not zero, same convention.
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/writablePercentageTotalDistribution
  data percentage_total_distribution_nonzero content boolean
  # Box 10. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableAmountAllocableToIRR
  data writable_amount_allocable_to_irr content money
  # Box 12. DF: /form1099Rs/*/factaFilingRequirement
  data facta_filing_requirement content boolean
  # Box 14 and the local tax box. DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableStateTaxWithheld
  data writable_state_tax_withheld content money
  # Box 15 answered "another state". DF: /form1099Rs/*/writablePayerState
  # equal to `differentState`
  data payer_state_is_different content boolean
  # A date of payment of a reportable death benefit is entered.
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableDateOfPayment is complete
  data has_death_benefit_payment_date content boolean
  # User answers to the box 7 follow-up screens.
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableIsIndirectRollover
  data writable_is_indirect_rollover content boolean
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableIsDistributionFromMilitaryRetirementPlan
  data writable_is_distribution_from_military_retirement_plan content boolean
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/writableQualifiedDisasterDistribution
  data writable_qualified_disaster_distribution content boolean
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/writeablePublicSafetyOfficer
  data writeable_public_safety_officer content boolean
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/writeablePublicSafetyOfficerPremiums
  data writeable_public_safety_officer_premiums content boolean
  # Date of birth of the recipient. DF: /form1099Rs/*/filer/dateOfBirth,
  # read by /form1099Rs/*/dateOfBirthBefore1936
  data recipient_date_of_birth content date
```

### Constants of this module

```catala-metadata
# DF: constants.xml /totalDistributionTaxableStartYear is the day 1936-01-02
# ("The date before which a TP cannot claim a total distribution on 1099-R in
# current scope"). The 1040 instructions (i1040gi--2024.pdf p 28, Lump-Sum
# Distributions) give the special treatment of a lump-sum distribution to a
# recipient "born before January 2, 1936".
declaration total_distribution_start_date content date equals |1936-01-02|
```

## The supported distribution codes

The 1040 instructions (`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 27)
say a "Form 1099-R" shows the pension and annuity payments in "box 1", and
that "Rollovers and lump-sum distributions are explained later". The meaning of
each box 7 code is in the Instructions for Forms 1099-R and 5498, which are not
in `sources/` (see the question in the PR). The codes this module accepts,
with the 2024 meaning from those instructions:

- `7` normal distribution;
- `2` early distribution, exception applies;
- `G` direct rollover of a distribution to a qualified plan, a section 403(b)
  plan, a governmental section 457(b) plan, or an IRA;
- `H` direct rollover of a designated Roth account distribution to a Roth IRA;
- the combinations `2B`, `7B` (with `B`, designated Roth account distribution),
  `BG`, `4G`, `4H` (`4`, death, with a direct rollover). The order of the two
  characters does not matter.

Any other box 7 content is unsupported: a different code (`1` early
distribution, `3` disability, `D`, `M`, ...), a supported code combined with
an unsupported one (`7D`, `7M`, `2D`), a repeated code, three or more
characters, or an empty box.

DF-BUG(1): Direct File first strips the typed code with
`StripChars(ToUpper(Trim(code)), "247BGH")` (`form1099Rs.xml` line 1251,
`constants.xml` line 915) and only then tests the whitelist
(`/form1099Rs/*/hasUnsupportedDistributionCode`, line 276). A code such as
`7D` is stripped to `7` and accepted although `7D` (normal distribution,
plus a different meaning for `D`) is not `7`. Here the whole code is tested
and `7D` is a knockout. No oracle scenario uses such a code, so there is no
known divergence in `oracle/facts.csv`.

```catala-metadata
## One 1099-R and everything the return reads from it.
declaration scope Form1099RItem:
  input form content Form1099R

  # Echo of `form.filer`, so a list of results can be filtered by filer.
  output filer content Types.FilerRole
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/grossDistribution (box 1, rounded)
  output gross_distribution content money
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/taxableAmount (box 2a, rounded)
  output taxable_amount content money
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/federalWithholding (box 4, rounded)
  output federal_withholding content money

  internal code_length content integer
  internal has_2 condition
  internal has_4 condition
  internal has_7 condition
  internal has_b condition
  internal has_g condition
  internal has_h condition

  # Exactly one of the supported codes of the previous section.
  # DF: negation of /form1099Rs/*/hasUnsupportedDistributionCode
  output has_supported_distribution_code condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/hasPensionRollover and /form1099Rs/*/isDirectRollover
  # (both: the code contains G or H)
  output is_direct_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/notIraSepSimple
  output not_ira_sep_simple condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/flowAskAboutIndirectRollover (the code contains 2 or 7
  # once only supported codes remain)
  output flow_ask_about_indirect_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/indicatedHasIndirectRollover
  output indicated_has_indirect_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/hasDistributionCodeIncludedInSaversCredit
  output has_distribution_code_included_in_savers_credit condition

  # DF: the Filter of /primaryFiler1099RsReportedOnSaversCredit:
  # code included and not `writableIsDistributionFromMilitaryRetirementPlan`
  output is_reported_on_savers_credit condition

  # Classification
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isTaxFreePensionRollover
  output is_tax_free_pension_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isTaxablePensionRollover
  output is_taxable_pension_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isIndirectRollover
  output is_indirect_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isTaxableAmountNotDetermined
  output is_taxable_amount_not_determined condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isFullyOrPartlyTaxablePension
  output is_fully_or_partly_taxable_pension condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isFullyTaxable
  output is_fully_taxable condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isPartlyTaxablePension
  output is_partly_taxable_pension condition

  # Knockouts, one per DF knockout fact (per form)
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/hasUnsupportedDistributionCode
  output ko_has_unsupported_distribution_code condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/iraSepSimple (counted by /knockoutIraSepSimple)
  output ko_ira_sep_simple condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isTaxablePensionRollover (/knockoutTaxablePensionRollover)
  output ko_taxable_pension_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isIndirectRollover (/knockoutIndirectRollover)
  output ko_indirect_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/isTaxableAmountNotDetermined
  # (/knockoutTaxableAmountNotDetermined)
  output ko_taxable_amount_not_determined condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesRolloverKO (/flowKnockoutForRollover)
  output ko_causes_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesPreTaxToPostTaxRolloverKO
  output ko_causes_pre_tax_to_post_tax_rollover condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/taxableAmountNotDetermined
  # (/flowKnockoutRetirementTaxableAmountNotDetermined)
  output ko_retirement_taxable_amount_not_determined condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesRetirementTaxableAmountNotDeterminedNotCheckedTaxableAmountBlankKO
  output ko_retirement_taxable_amount_blank condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesRetirementTotalDistributionKO
  output ko_retirement_total_distribution condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesRetirementBox8ValueKO
  output ko_box_8_value condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesRetirementBox8PercentageKO
  output ko_box_8_percentage condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesRetirementBox9aPercentageKO
  output ko_box_9a_percentage condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesRetirementCapitalGainKO
  output ko_capital_gain condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesRetirementNetUnrealizedAppreciation
  output ko_net_unrealized_appreciation condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesRetirementAmountAllocableToIRRKO
  output ko_amount_allocable_to_irr condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/factaFilingRequirement (/flowKnockoutRetirementFactaFilingRequirement)
  output ko_facta_filing_requirement condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesDeathBenefitPaymentKO
  output ko_death_benefit_payment condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/qualifiedDisasterDistribution
  # (/flowKnockoutRetirementQualifiedDisasterDistribution)
  output ko_qualified_disaster_distribution condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesPSOPremiumsKnockout
  # (/flowKnockoutRetirementPublicSafetyOfficer)
  output ko_public_safety_officer_premiums condition
  # DF: /form1099Rs/*/causesBox15Knockout (/flowKnockoutBox15)
  output ko_box_15 condition
  # Any of the above
  output unsupported condition
```

### Box amounts

DF rounds boxes 1, 2a and 4 on their own (`Round` around a `Switch` that
falls back to `$0`; with complete inputs the `Switch` is the box itself).

```catala
scope Form1099RItem:
  definition filer equals form.filer

  # QUIRK(Q-R1): per-item rounding. DF: form1099Rs.xml
  # /form1099Rs/*/grossDistribution. Decision: reproduce (conventions
  # section 4 rule 2, issue #60).
  definition gross_distribution equals
    R.round_dollar of form.writable_gross_distribution
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/taxableAmount
  definition taxable_amount equals
    R.round_dollar of form.writable_taxable_amount
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/federalWithholding
  definition federal_withholding equals
    R.round_dollar of form.writable_federal_withholding
```

### The code, tested as a whole

```catala
scope Form1099RItem:
  definition code_length equals
    Integer.sum of (map each c among form.distribution_code to 1)
  definition has_2 equals
    exists c among form.distribution_code such that c = CodeChar.Code2
  definition has_4 equals
    exists c among form.distribution_code such that c = CodeChar.Code4
  definition has_7 equals
    exists c among form.distribution_code such that c = CodeChar.Code7
  definition has_b equals
    exists c among form.distribution_code such that c = CodeChar.CodeB
  definition has_g equals
    exists c among form.distribution_code such that c = CodeChar.CodeG
  definition has_h equals
    exists c among form.distribution_code such that c = CodeChar.CodeH

  # DF-BUG(1): see the section "The supported distribution codes". DF's list
  # is 2, 7, G, H, 2B, B2, 7B, B7, BG, GB, 4G, G4, 4H, H4; it is the same set,
  # here as "one character" or "two distinct characters" so the order is free.
  # A code with a character that is not one of the six (OtherCode) matches
  # none of the cases, so `7D` is unsupported.
  definition has_supported_distribution_code equals
    (code_length = 1 and (has_2 or has_7 or has_g or has_h))
    or (code_length = 2 and
        ((has_2 and has_b) or (has_7 and has_b) or (has_b and has_g)
         or (has_4 and has_g) or (has_4 and has_h)))

  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/isDirectRollover:
  # `Length(StripChars(distributionCode, "GH")) > 0`.
  definition is_direct_rollover equals has_g or has_h

  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/notIraSepSimple
  definition not_ira_sep_simple equals not form.ira_sep_simple

  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/flowAskAboutIndirectRollover:
  # `Length(StripChars(distributionCode, "1237")) > 0`. After the whole-code
  # test only the characters 2 and 7 can make it true.
  definition flow_ask_about_indirect_rollover equals has_2 or has_7

  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/indicatedHasIndirectRollover (a Switch
  # with only the "ask" case; incomplete otherwise, read as false)
  definition indicated_has_indirect_rollover equals
    flow_ask_about_indirect_rollover and form.writable_is_indirect_rollover

  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/hasDistributionCodeIncludedInSaversCredit:
  # the codes 2, 7, 2B, B2, 7B, B7. Form 8880 instructions line 4
  # (f8880--2024.pdf p 2): "Don't include ... Distributions not taxable as the
  # result of a rollover", so G and H forms are left out.
  definition has_distribution_code_included_in_savers_credit equals
    (code_length = 1 and (has_2 or has_7))
    or (code_length = 2 and has_b and (has_2 or has_7))

  # DF: saversCredits.xml filters on this and on the military answer.
  definition is_reported_on_savers_credit equals
    has_distribution_code_included_in_savers_credit
    and not form.writable_is_distribution_from_military_retirement_plan
```

### Classification: rollover, fully taxable, partly taxable

1040 instructions lines 5a and 5b (`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf`
p 28): "If your pension or annuity is fully taxable, enter the total pension or
annuity payments (from Form(s) 1099-R, box 1) on line 5b; don't make an entry
on line 5a." and, for a partially taxable one, "Enter the total pension or
annuity payments" on line 5a and the taxable part on line 5b.

DF decides from box 7 and the amounts: a form without IRA/SEP/SIMPLE that has a
direct rollover code and a taxable amount of `$0` is a tax-free pension
rollover; the same with a taxable amount above `$0` is a taxable rollover
(knockout). For the other supported codes the form is fully taxable when box 1
equals box 2a and partly taxable otherwise.

```catala
scope Form1099RItem:
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/isTaxFreePensionRollover
  definition is_tax_free_pension_rollover equals
    not_ira_sep_simple and is_direct_rollover and taxable_amount = $0
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/isTaxablePensionRollover
  definition is_taxable_pension_rollover equals
    not_ira_sep_simple and is_direct_rollover and taxable_amount > $0
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/isIndirectRollover
  definition is_indirect_rollover equals
    not_ira_sep_simple and not is_direct_rollover
    and indicated_has_indirect_rollover
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/isTaxableAmountNotDetermined
  definition is_taxable_amount_not_determined equals
    not_ira_sep_simple and not is_direct_rollover
    and form.taxable_amount_not_determined
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/isFullyOrPartlyTaxablePension
  definition is_fully_or_partly_taxable_pension equals
    not form.ira_sep_simple and not is_taxable_amount_not_determined
    and not is_indirect_rollover
    and has_distribution_code_included_in_savers_credit
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/isFullyTaxable
  definition is_fully_taxable equals
    is_fully_or_partly_taxable_pension and gross_distribution = taxable_amount
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099Rs/*/isPartlyTaxablePension
  definition is_partly_taxable_pension equals
    is_fully_or_partly_taxable_pension and gross_distribution != taxable_amount
```

### Knockouts of one form

Each of these is one of the DF knockout facts of `flow.xml`
(`/flowIsKnockedOut`), restricted to one form; the scope below ORs them over
the forms. The facts for codes `1` and `3` (`/form1099Rs/*/flowQualifiedEarlyDistribution`,
`hasDisabilityAndAnotherCode`) are dead code in DF: its stripped code can never
be `1` or `3`. Here code `1`, `3` and any combination with them are not
supported at all (`ko_has_unsupported_distribution_code`), which is the
behaviour they were written for, so no separate conditions exist for them.

```catala
scope Form1099RItem:
  rule ko_has_unsupported_distribution_code
    under condition not has_supported_distribution_code
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_ira_sep_simple under condition form.ira_sep_simple
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_taxable_pension_rollover under condition is_taxable_pension_rollover
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_indirect_rollover under condition is_indirect_rollover
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_taxable_amount_not_determined
    under condition is_taxable_amount_not_determined
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: causesRolloverKO: indicated and answered "yes, indirect rollover".
  rule ko_causes_rollover under condition indicated_has_indirect_rollover
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: causesPreTaxToPostTaxRolloverKO: a pension rollover code with a
  # taxable amount above $0 (not conditioned on IRA/SEP/SIMPLE).
  rule ko_causes_pre_tax_to_post_tax_rollover
    under condition is_direct_rollover and taxable_amount > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_retirement_taxable_amount_not_determined
    under condition form.taxable_amount_not_determined
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_retirement_taxable_amount_blank
    under condition form.taxable_amount_blank
      and not form.taxable_amount_not_determined
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: dateOfBirthBefore1936 is `totalDistributionTaxableStartYear >
  # filer/dateOfBirth`, i.e. born before 1936-01-02.
  rule ko_retirement_total_distribution
    under condition form.total_distribution
      and form.recipient_date_of_birth < total_distribution_start_date
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: roundedOtherDollar > 0
  rule ko_box_8_value
    under condition (R.round_dollar of form.writable_other_dollar) > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF-BUG(7, proposed): DF tests "box 8 percentage is zero" on the typed text
  # with `StripChars(text, "0.")`. The XML literal `<String>0.</String>` is
  # read by the fast-xml-parser setting used by the Direct File client and by
  # `oracle/generate.mjs` (no `parseTagValue: false`) as the number `0`, i.e.
  # the string "0", so "0.00" loses its dots and looks nonzero: the percentage
  # knockout fires for a box 8 of "0.00" (the four oracle scenarios
  # `1099r-box-2b-total-distribution`, `ats-2-1099r`,
  # `ats-2-1099r-blank-taxable`, `ats-2-1099r-nonzero-taxable`). A percentage
  # of zero is zero: here it is a knockout only when nonzero (the input
  # `other_percentage_nonzero`). Box 9a ("0") is not affected.
  rule ko_box_8_percentage under condition form.other_percentage_nonzero
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_box_9a_percentage
    under condition form.percentage_total_distribution_nonzero
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_capital_gain
    under condition (R.round_dollar of form.writable_capital_gain) > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_net_unrealized_appreciation
    under condition (R.round_dollar of form.writable_net_appreciation) > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_amount_allocable_to_irr
    under condition
      (R.round_dollar of form.writable_amount_allocable_to_irr) > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_facta_filing_requirement under condition form.facta_filing_requirement
    consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_death_benefit_payment under condition form.has_death_benefit_payment_date
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: qualifiedDisasterDistribution is the answer only when the
  # indirect-rollover screen is asked.
  rule ko_qualified_disaster_distribution
    under condition flow_ask_about_indirect_rollover
      and form.writable_qualified_disaster_distribution
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: the public safety officer screen is asked when the code contains 2 or
  # 7 and no B; the premiums screen when the answer is yes.
  rule ko_public_safety_officer_premiums
    under condition (has_2 or has_7) and not has_b
      and form.writeable_public_safety_officer
      and form.writeable_public_safety_officer_premiums
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: causesBox15Knockout: "another state" and (state tax above $0 or no
  # rollover code). The check is on the rounded Box 14.
  rule ko_box_15
    under condition form.payer_state_is_different
      and ((R.round_dollar of form.writable_state_tax_withheld) > $0
           or not is_direct_rollover)
    consequence fulfilled

  rule unsupported under condition
    ko_has_unsupported_distribution_code or ko_ira_sep_simple
    or ko_taxable_pension_rollover or ko_indirect_rollover
    or ko_taxable_amount_not_determined or ko_causes_rollover
    or ko_causes_pre_tax_to_post_tax_rollover
    or ko_retirement_taxable_amount_not_determined
    or ko_retirement_taxable_amount_blank or ko_retirement_total_distribution
    or ko_box_8_value or ko_box_8_percentage or ko_box_9a_percentage
    or ko_capital_gain or ko_net_unrealized_appreciation
    or ko_amount_allocable_to_irr or ko_facta_filing_requirement
    or ko_death_benefit_payment or ko_qualified_disaster_distribution
    or ko_public_safety_officer_premiums or ko_box_15
    consequence fulfilled
```

## The scope over all forms

```catala-metadata
## All Forms 1099-R of the return.
declaration scope Form1099Rs:
  ## DF: /form1099Rs
  input forms content list of Form1099R

  internal items content list of Form1099RItem
  internal primary_items content list of Form1099RItem
  internal secondary_items content list of Form1099RItem
  internal tax_free_rollover_items content list of Form1099RItem
  internal partly_taxable_items content list of Form1099RItem
  internal fully_taxable_items content list of Form1099RItem

  # DF: /taxFreePensionRollovers
  output tax_free_pension_rollovers content money
  # DF: /partlyTaxablePensions
  output partly_taxable_pensions content money
  # DF: /fullyTaxablePensions
  output fully_taxable_pensions content money
  # DF: /taxableAmountsOfPartiallyTaxablePensions
  output taxable_amounts_of_partially_taxable_pensions content money

  # Form 1040 line 5a. DF: income.xml /pensionsAndAnnuities
  output line_5a content money
  # Form 1040 line 5b. DF: income.xml /taxablePensionsAndAnnuities
  output line_5b content money
  # DF: income.xml /taxablePensionsAndAnnuitiesDisplay is blank (incomplete)
  # exactly when this is true: line 5b is $0 and no form is a tax-free rollover.
  output line_5b_is_blank condition
  # DF: income.xml /taxablePensionsAndAnnuitiesLiteralCode is "ROLLOVER".
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /has1099RWithDirectRollover
  output has_direct_rollover condition
  # DF: income.xml /nonTaxablePensionsAndAnnuities (Schedule R)
  output non_taxable_pensions_and_annuities content money

  # Form 1040 line 25b, 1099-R part. DF: /form1099RsFederalIncomeTaxWithheld
  output form_1099r_federal_income_tax_withheld content money

  # Form 8880 line 4, per filer.
  # DF: /primaryFiler1099RsReportedOnSaversCredit (sum of grossDistribution)
  output primary_filer_savers_gross_distributions content money
  # DF: /secondaryFiler1099RsReportedOnSaversCredit (sum of grossDistribution)
  output secondary_filer_savers_gross_distributions content money

  # Knockouts, one per DF knockout fact (conventions section 6)
  # DF: /knockoutForForm1099RDistributionCode
  output ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_distribution_code condition
  # DF: /knockoutIraSepSimple
  output ko_knockout_ira_sep_simple condition
  # DF: /knockoutTaxablePensionRollover
  output ko_knockout_taxable_pension_rollover condition
  # DF: /knockoutIndirectRollover
  output ko_knockout_indirect_rollover condition
  # DF: /knockoutTaxableAmountNotDetermined
  output ko_knockout_taxable_amount_not_determined condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutForRollover
  output ko_flow_knockout_for_rollover condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutForPreTaxToPostTaxRollover
  output ko_flow_knockout_for_pre_tax_to_post_tax_rollover condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutRetirementTaxableAmountNotDetermined
  output ko_flow_knockout_retirement_taxable_amount_not_determined condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutRetirementTaxableAmountNotDeterminedNotCheckedTaxableAmountBlank
  output ko_flow_knockout_retirement_taxable_amount_blank condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutRetirementTotalDistribution
  output ko_flow_knockout_retirement_total_distribution condition
  # DF: /knockoutForForm1099RBox8Value
  output ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_box8_value condition
  # DF: /knockoutForForm1099RBox8Percentage
  output ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_box8_percentage condition
  # DF: /knockoutForForm1099RBox9aPercentage
  output ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_box9a_percentage condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutRetirementCapitalGain
  output ko_flow_knockout_retirement_capital_gain condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutRetirementNetUnrealizedAppreciation
  output ko_flow_knockout_retirement_net_unrealized_appreciation condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutRetirementAmountAllocableToIRR
  output ko_flow_knockout_retirement_amount_allocable_to_irr condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutRetirementFactaFilingRequirement
  output ko_flow_knockout_retirement_facta_filing_requirement condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutForDeathBenefitPaymentDate
  output ko_flow_knockout_for_death_benefit_payment_date condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutRetirementQualifiedDisasterDistribution
  output ko_flow_knockout_retirement_qualified_disaster_distribution condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutRetirementPublicSafetyOfficer
  output ko_flow_knockout_retirement_public_safety_officer condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutBox15
  output ko_flow_knockout_box15 condition
  # Every knockout above
  output unsupported condition
```

```catala
scope Form1099Rs:
  definition items equals
    map each f among forms to (output of Form1099RItem with { -- form: f })
  definition primary_items equals
    list of x among items such that x.filer = Types.FilerRole.PrimaryFiler
  definition secondary_items equals
    list of x among items such that x.filer = Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition tax_free_rollover_items equals
    list of x among items such that x.is_tax_free_pension_rollover
  definition partly_taxable_items equals
    list of x among items such that x.is_partly_taxable_pension
  definition fully_taxable_items equals
    list of x among items such that x.is_fully_taxable
```

### Lines 5a and 5b

Form 1040 line 5a is "Pensions and annuities" and line 5b "Taxable amount"
(`sources/forms-instructions/f1040--2024.pdf` p 1). DF: line 5a is the gross
distributions of the tax-free rollovers and of the partly taxable pensions;
line 5b is the gross distributions of the fully taxable pensions plus the taxable
amounts of the partly taxable ones. All terms are sums of whole dollars, so DF
adds no extra `Round`.

```catala
scope Form1099Rs:
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /taxFreePensionRollovers
  definition tax_free_pension_rollovers equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among tax_free_rollover_items
                  to x.gross_distribution)
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /partlyTaxablePensions
  definition partly_taxable_pensions equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among partly_taxable_items
                  to x.gross_distribution)
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /fullyTaxablePensions
  definition fully_taxable_pensions equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among fully_taxable_items
                  to x.gross_distribution)
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /taxableAmountsOfPartiallyTaxablePensions
  definition taxable_amounts_of_partially_taxable_pensions equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among partly_taxable_items to x.taxable_amount)

  # QUIRK(Q1): DF's line 5a omits the fully taxable pensions
  # (`income.xml` `/pensionsAndAnnuities` = `taxFreePensionRollovers` +
  # `partlyTaxablePensions`). The 1040 instructions agree (i1040gi--2024.pdf
  # p 28: "If your pension or annuity is fully taxable, enter the total pension
  # or annuity payments (from Form(s) 1099-R, box 1) on line 5b; don't make an
  # entry on line 5a."), so this is not a divergence: policy and oracle choose
  # the same value. The partly taxable pension's gross goes on line 5a; the
  # rollover gross goes on line 5a with "ROLLOVER" next to line 5b.
  # DF: income.xml /pensionsAndAnnuities
  definition line_5a equals
    tax_free_pension_rollovers + partly_taxable_pensions
  # DF: income.xml /taxablePensionsAndAnnuities
  definition line_5b equals
    fully_taxable_pensions + taxable_amounts_of_partially_taxable_pensions

  # DF: income.xml /taxablePensionsAndAnnuitiesDisplay: 5b if above $0; else
  # $0 if some form is a tax-free rollover; else left blank.
  definition line_5b_is_blank equals
    not (line_5b > $0) and not (exists x among items such that
                                 x.is_tax_free_pension_rollover)
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /has1099RWithDirectRollover
  definition has_direct_rollover equals
    exists x among items such that x.is_direct_rollover
  # DF: income.xml /nonTaxablePensionsAndAnnuities = line 5a - line 5b
  definition non_taxable_pensions_and_annuities equals line_5a - line_5b
```

### Line 25b and Form 8880 line 4

DF: `/form1099RsFederalIncomeTaxWithheld` is the sum of the per-form rounded box
4 amounts (the `Switch` on `/form1099Rs` completeness falls back to `$0`; with
complete inputs it is the sum). Form 1040 line 25b, "Form(s) 1099", is the sum
of this and the withholding of the other 1099s (`taxCalculations.xml`
`/form1099Withholding`, wired in `Form1040`).

Form 8880 line 4 instructions (`sources/forms-instructions/f8880--2024.pdf`
p 2): "Enter the total amount of distributions you, and your spouse if filing
jointly, received after 2021 and before the due date of your 2024 return
(including extensions) from any of the following types of plans." and "Don't
include ... Distributions from a military retirement plan (other than the
federal TSP)." DF's per-filer sums (`saversCredits.xml`
`/primaryFilerSaversEligibleGrossDistributions`, which also asks whether the
filer is eligible for the credit, left to #29) add up `grossDistribution` of
the filer's forms with code 2, 7, 2B, B2, 7B or B7 that are not from a
military retirement plan.

```catala
scope Form1099Rs:
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /form1099RsFederalIncomeTaxWithheld
  definition form_1099r_federal_income_tax_withheld equals
    Money.sum of (map each x among items to x.federal_withholding)

  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /primaryFiler1099RsReportedOnSaversCredit
  definition primary_filer_savers_gross_distributions equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each x among
         (list of y among primary_items such that y.is_reported_on_savers_credit)
       to x.gross_distribution)
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /secondaryFiler1099RsReportedOnSaversCredit
  definition secondary_filer_savers_gross_distributions equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each x among
         (list of y among secondary_items such that
            y.is_reported_on_savers_credit)
       to x.gross_distribution)
```

### Knockouts

Conventions section 6: one `ko_` condition per DF knockout fact, and one
`unsupported` that lists them all. The DF facts count the forms where the
per-form condition holds, so each is an `exists`.

```catala
scope Form1099Rs:
  rule ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_distribution_code
    under condition exists x among items such that
      x.ko_has_unsupported_distribution_code
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_knockout_ira_sep_simple
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_ira_sep_simple
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_knockout_taxable_pension_rollover
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_taxable_pension_rollover
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_knockout_indirect_rollover
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_indirect_rollover
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_knockout_taxable_amount_not_determined
    under condition exists x among items such that
      x.ko_taxable_amount_not_determined
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_for_rollover
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_causes_rollover
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_for_pre_tax_to_post_tax_rollover
    under condition exists x among items such that
      x.ko_causes_pre_tax_to_post_tax_rollover
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_retirement_taxable_amount_not_determined
    under condition exists x among items such that
      x.ko_retirement_taxable_amount_not_determined
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_retirement_taxable_amount_blank
    under condition exists x among items such that
      x.ko_retirement_taxable_amount_blank
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_retirement_total_distribution
    under condition exists x among items such that
      x.ko_retirement_total_distribution
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_box8_value
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_box_8_value
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_box8_percentage
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_box_8_percentage
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_box9a_percentage
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_box_9a_percentage
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_retirement_capital_gain
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_capital_gain
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_retirement_net_unrealized_appreciation
    under condition exists x among items such that
      x.ko_net_unrealized_appreciation
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_retirement_amount_allocable_to_irr
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_amount_allocable_to_irr
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_retirement_facta_filing_requirement
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_facta_filing_requirement
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_for_death_benefit_payment_date
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_death_benefit_payment
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_retirement_qualified_disaster_distribution
    under condition exists x among items such that
      x.ko_qualified_disaster_distribution
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_retirement_public_safety_officer
    under condition exists x among items such that
      x.ko_public_safety_officer_premiums
    consequence fulfilled
  rule ko_flow_knockout_box15
    under condition exists x among items such that x.ko_box_15
    consequence fulfilled

  rule unsupported under condition
    ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_distribution_code or ko_knockout_ira_sep_simple
    or ko_knockout_taxable_pension_rollover or ko_knockout_indirect_rollover
    or ko_knockout_taxable_amount_not_determined or ko_flow_knockout_for_rollover
    or ko_flow_knockout_for_pre_tax_to_post_tax_rollover
    or ko_flow_knockout_retirement_taxable_amount_not_determined
    or ko_flow_knockout_retirement_taxable_amount_blank
    or ko_flow_knockout_retirement_total_distribution
    or ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_box8_value
    or ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_box8_percentage
    or ko_knockout_for_form1099_r_box9a_percentage
    or ko_flow_knockout_retirement_capital_gain
    or ko_flow_knockout_retirement_net_unrealized_appreciation
    or ko_flow_knockout_retirement_amount_allocable_to_irr
    or ko_flow_knockout_retirement_facta_filing_requirement
    or ko_flow_knockout_for_death_benefit_payment_date
    or ko_flow_knockout_retirement_qualified_disaster_distribution
    or ko_flow_knockout_retirement_public_safety_officer
    or ko_flow_knockout_box15
    consequence fulfilled
```
